# No dead code in touched changes

When you add or edit code, **do not leave** dead stubs, unused symbols, or
duplicate gates in the paths you change. Clean them in the **same** change (same
bar as no-legacy: one clear contract, no leftovers “just in case”).

## Delete or finish — do not park

| Smell | Example | Action |
| ----- | ------- | ------ |
| Stub / no-op predicate | `function c() { return true; }` (or always-false) still used as a gate | Replace with real logic, or delete and simplify call sites |
| Thin rename wrapper | `function a(args) { return b(args); }` | Delete `a`; callers use `b` (see `no-legacy-code`) |
| Pass-through re-export after move | `export { A } from './new-file'` only to keep old import path | Point imports at the real module; drop the barrel unless it **is** the public API |
| Redundant double-check | `test(x)` already calls `test2()`, then caller checks `test2()` again | One source of truth for the gate |
| Unused export / orphan helper | Exported or file-local helper never referenced after the refactor | Remove it (or wire it — do not leave orphans) |
| Commented-out old implementation | Old body left beside the new one | Delete the dead block |

## Scope

- Applies to **files you touched** this task — do not drive-by-delete unrelated
  debt elsewhere.
- Tests may keep deliberate stubs/fakes; name them clearly (`createFake…`,
  `stubTransport`). Do not ship production `return true` gates “temporarily”.
- Exception only if the **user explicitly** asks to keep a shim/stub; note that
  in the summary and prefer a removal follow-up.

## Before handoff

Quick pass on your diff: any new function/export unused? any always-true/false
helper? any check duplicated up the call stack? Fix before `ci:check` / review.

Reviewer hygiene (same patterns): `.cursor/agents/wordreapers-staged-reviewer.md`.
